<title>USA: International Game sells 650 machines.</title>
<headline>International Game sells 650 machines.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Game Technology said Monday that its International Game Technology-Africa (Pty) Ltd unit has signed a pact with MGM Grand Inc's partner, Tsogo Sun, for the purchase of 650 gaming machines.</p>
<p>The pact also calls for the purchase of two of IGT's SMART player tracking systems. All will be installed in Tsogo Sun's two temporary casinos in Mpumalanga, South Africa.</p>
<p>IGT, based in Nevada, said the South African national gaming act passed in July 1996 permits the allocation of 40 licenses throughout the nine provinces of South Africa.</p>
<p>It said Mpumalanga is the first province to award its casino licenses.</p>
</text>
